  "preamble": "Allophonic aspiration of voiceless /k/ to [kʰ] in the onset of a stressed syllable. In English the two variants are in complementary distribution: aspirated word-initially and stressed-syllable-initially, unaspirated after /s/. Turkish likewise usually aspirates syllable-initial /p, t, c, k/. As a historical change, plain *k became kʰ in Chong (Proto-Pearic *kam 'arrow' > kʰam) and in Proto-Khasian (*kaʔ 'fish' > *kʰa), while the old voiced stops devoiced to plain stops, a register-type split.",
